  "body": "Stacked on #1434 (the DNM travel fix, #1410): this branch is cut from `issue/1410-doosan-travel`, so its diff against `main` holds #1434's commit until that merges. The commit that belongs to this PR is the last one.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe built-in DNM 5700 declared the catalog's *optional* 4th-axis table (`rot_a`) with no `nose_to_axis`, so the index-swing law (`posting_index_swing.rs`) refused every op on it, plain 3-axis work at A0 included. I took the issue's option 2 and invented no figure. The safety law is not touched.\n\n- `assets/machines/doosan-dnm-3axis.mch` (new) is the built-in **\"Doosan DNM 5700\"**: the same catalog figures and #1410's strokes, with no A. A 3-axis job now posts.\n- `assets/machines/doosan-dnm.mch` keeps the A table and becomes the built-in **\"Doosan DNM 5700 + rotary table\"**. Its `general.model` was renamed to match, so the program header reads `(Doosan DNM 5700 + rotary table)`. It still states no `nose_to_axis`, so every op on it is refused by name until the setup states its own (`SetSetupNoseToAxis` / MCP `set_setup_nose_to_axis`).\n- `posting::MACHINES` lists both. This follows the `Tormach 770MX` / `Tormach 770MX + microARC 4` precedent.\n- Old projects: a project file embeds its mounted machine, so a project saved on the old \"Doosan DNM 5700\" keeps its A table and refuses exactly as before. Remounting the built-in gives the 3-axis machine.\n- The A-table file keeps its path, so the post tests, conformance, `doosan_dnm_a_state` and `program_units` read it unchanged. Only the library name and the header changed in `fourth_axis_pose.rs`, `machine.rs` (catalog pin) and `doosan_dnm_post.rs` (header assert).\n- Docs: the rotary table in `site/content/guide/multi-axis/_index.md`. Decision: `docs/decisions/1433-dnm-3axis-split.md`.\n\nNo new command, so no MCP tool is owed.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests in `crates/app/tests/vmc_stroke.rs`:\n- `a_plate_contour_on_the_built_in_dnm_passes_the_stroke_and_posts`: the plain DNM has no rotary, the verification report is empty, and `post_setup` succeeds. Before this change, the test asserted that the nose refusal was the only problem.\n- `the_dnm_rotary_variant_still_refuses_an_unjudgeable_index_by_name` (new): the variant states its A with no `nose_to_axis`, the report names `2D Contour1: Doosan DNM 5700 + rotary table ... states no nose_to_axis`, and `post_setup` errors.\n\n**Mutation check (standing rule):**\n- Pointing \"Doosan DNM 5700\" back at the A-table file made `a_plate_contour_on_the_built_in_dnm_passes_the_stroke_and_posts` fail (RED). Restoring it made it pass (GREEN).\n- Deleting the `Nose::Unstated` refusal push in `posting_index_swing.rs` made `the_dnm_rotary_variant_still_refuses_an_unjudgeable_index_by_name` fail (RED). Restoring it made it pass (GREEN).\n\nQuick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, post suites (doosan_dnm_post, probe_spindle_stop) ok in 31 s and the gate-mapped app suites (vmc_stroke, machine, machine_library, fourth_axis_pose, conformance, doosan_dnm_a_state, program_units, index_swing, ...) ok in 371 s; 0 failed, wall 6.7 min.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The UI machine picker was not driven by hand. The picker lists `MACHINES`, and `machine.rs` / `machine_library.rs` pin that.\n- Snapshot PNGs are untouched.\n\nChangelog: The built-in Doosan DNM 5700 is now plain 3-axis and posts 3-axis work; its optional A table is a separate built-in \"Doosan DNM 5700 + rotary table\" that refuses by name until the setup states its nose_to_axis (#1433)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nfork synced at v0.19.0\n\nFixes #1433\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
